  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In the first step bromine attacks the carbon-carbon double bond by electrophilic addition reaction mechanism and forms the bromonium&nbsp;cyclic intermediate. In the presence of sodium bicarbonate carboxylic acid group present in the reactant&nbsp;converts to carboxylate ion. This carboxylate ion opens the cyclic bromonium ion ring and forms the desired product.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bdaeac43-97bd-4440-b424-f4895151620b-image.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 228px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
